<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2630" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ănĭmōsĭtas</span></b> ,
			ātis, f.
		animosus (only post-class.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Boldness</i>, <i>courage</i>, <i>spirit</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">resistendi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 16, 12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">equi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 4, 3</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Vehemence</i>, <i>impetuosity</i>,
				<i>ardor</i>, <i><span class="en">Macr. Somn.
				Scip. 1, 6</span></i>; in plur., *
					<i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aug. Ep.
				162</span></i>, and Civ. Dei, 14, 2 al.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>Wrath</i>, <i>enmity</i> (eccl.
			Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">iracundia animositatis illius (Dei) subversio
					illius est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Eccli. 1, 28</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">ib. 2 Cor. 12, 20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">ib. Heb. 11,
				27</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
